<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Silesian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1744–1745</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-austrian-succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Silesian War (1744–1745) was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, as part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-austrian-succession">War of the Austrian Succession</a>. Fearing Austria would retake Silesia, Frederick II invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> in 1744 and then won the battles of Hohenfriedberg, Soor and Kesselsdorf in 1745. The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dresden">Dresden</a> of December 1745 confirmed Prussian possession of Silesia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-silesian-war.jpg" alt="Second Silesian War" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carl Röchling · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hohenfriedeberg_-_Attack_of_Prussian_Infantry_-_1745.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
